{"name":"Tide Whisper","hex":"#fff6de","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tide","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The daily fluctuation in the level of the sea caused by the gravitational influence of the moon and the sun.","The associated flow of water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause to float with the tide; to drive or carry with the tide or stream.","To carry over or through a problem or difficulty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tide"},{"term":"whisper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of speaking in a quiet voice, especially without vibration of the vocal cords; the sound thus produced.","A rumor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To speak softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter words without sonant breath; to talk without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound.","To say (something) softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter (something) without sonant breath, without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tide","blocks":[{"text":"Tides are the periodic rise and fall of sea level resulting from the differential gravitational forces exerted primarily by the Moon and the Sun, combined with inertial effects associated with the Earth–Moon system’s orbital motion and the Earth's rotation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Tide_overview.svg/330px-Tide_overview.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tide","wikidata":"Q23384"},{"title":"Whispering","blocks":[{"text":"Whispering is an unvoiced mode of phonation in which the vocal cords are abducted so that they do not vibrate; air passes between the arytenoid cartilages to create audible turbulence during speech. Supralaryngeal articulation remains the same as in normal speech."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whispering","wikidata":"Q1434962"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png/120px-High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png/250px-High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png/120px-High_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHigh_tide_sun_moon_same_side_beginning.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png/120px-Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png/250px-Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png/120px-Low_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALow_tide_sun_moon_90_degrees.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/High_tide_sun_moon_opposite_side.png/120px-High_tide_sun_moon_opposite_side.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/High_tide_sun_moon_opposite_side.png/250px-High_tide_sun_m